        example: b"error fix.usage: --only takes imports, unused, pub, unsafe, suggested, tidy-imports, reexports, std015, values, conventions, conventions-spelling, unneeded-unsafe, unneeded-justified, obsolete-attr, usize, fstring, casts, casts-list, alloc, buf, rawptr or rawptr-list, not 'import'",
    },
    Explain {
        code: b"fix.alloc016-manual", severity: b"error, exit 1 (the rest is fixed)",
        means: b"`fix --only alloc016` threads `gpa: Gpa` from `fn main(gpa: Gpa)` to every call of \
            std's 0.15 allocating forms, but this function cannot take a parameter: it implements \
            a trait of std (`Display::fmt`), it is used as a value (`apply(make)`), or the call is \
            a parameter's default. It and the functions only it calls are left as they were.",
        fix: b"Keep a `gpa: Gpa` in the value the function works on (a field set where the value \
